# KNOX Vault — Agent Instructions

This vault is a **KNOX** knowledge base. It produces **OKF v0.2** (Open Knowledge
Format) bundles — a directory of markdown files with YAML frontmatter.

## Quick Reference

| Action | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Compile sources into wiki | `knox compile` |
| Ingest new documents | `knox ingest <files>` |
| Query the compiled wiki | `knox query <question>` |
| Capture knowledge from conversation | `knox capture <text>` |
| Store a fact verbatim | `knox learn <text>` |
| Check vault health | `knox status` |
| Start ACP agent (credential-free LLM) | `knox agent` |
| Start MCP server | `knox mcp` |

## OKF v0.2 Conformance

- Every concept file has parseable YAML frontmatter with a non-empty `type` field
- Trust fields: `generated: {by, at}` (supersedes v0.1 `timestamp`), `status`
- Cross-links use absolute bundle-relative paths: `[Title](/concepts/title.md)`
- Reserved filenames (`index.md`, `log.md`) follow OKF structure
- Root `index.md` declares `okf_version: "0.2"`
- `log.md` uses ISO 8601 date headings with bold action prefix
- Per-claim attribution via footnotes `[^id]` keyed to structured `sources[].id`

## ACP Agent Mode

KNOX implements the Agent Client Protocol (ACP). To inject your LLM endpoint
without sharing credentials, start KNOX as an ACP agent:

```bash
knox agent
```

The editor calls `providers/set` to configure the LLM, then sends `/knox <command>`
slash commands. See `knox agent --help` for details.

## Directory Layout

```
.                       ← vault root
├── index.md           ← vault-root hub → wiki catalog
├── .knox/              ← derived state ONLY (cache, vectors, search db, memory) — never required to read the wiki
├── sources/            ← source documents (PDF, DOCX, markdown, URLs)
│   ├── _captured/      ← knowledge items extracted from conversation
│   └── _distilled/     ← LLM-synthesized wiki pages
├── attachments/        ← durable media (per-source attachments + wiki-embedded images)
├── exported/           ← full-source markdown exports (on demand, reference only)
└── wiki/               ← compiled output (OKF v0.2 bundle)
    ├── index.md        ← portable catalog — links EVERYTHING the wiki generates
    ├── log.md          ← change log
    ├── references.md   ← corpus sources + cited works not in corpus (always present)
    ├── quality.md      ← claim verification summary (if a verify pass ran)
    ├── summaries/      ← one page per ingested source (assets, citations, backlinks)
    ├── entities/       ← entity pages (standards, organizations, products, people)
    └── concepts/       ← concept/comparison pages
```

## No knox available? Navigate the wiki yourself

If you cannot use the knox CLI or MCP (no install, no credentials, or the
vault was shared without `.knox/`), the wiki is still fully usable — it is
complete in its markdown pages:

1. **Entry point:** `wiki/index.md` — the portable catalog. It links every
   generated page group plus `references.md`, `summaries/`, `quality.md`,
   `log.md`.
2. **Concepts:** `wiki/concepts/*.md` — one page per topic, with Related
   sections, source-file provenance, and per-claim footnotes. Entity pages
   live in `wiki/entities/*.md`.
3. **Per-source detail:** `wiki/summaries/<source>.md` — asset inventory,
   extracted citations, and backlinks to the concepts a source feeds.
4. **Trust:** `wiki/quality.md` (when present) — per-page claim verification
   table; concept frontmatter carries `verified_claims` / `quality_score`.
5. **Media:** image embeds point into `attachments/` — they render in any
   markdown viewer.

Everything reachable from `wiki/index.md` is the complete knowledge surface;
`.knox/` is regenerable derived state and never needed for reading.

## Configuration

Config lives in `.knox/config.toml`. Key settings:

| Key | Default | Purpose |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `compile.llm.default_model` | `""` | LLM for compilation/querying (required) |
| `compile.llm.vlm_model` | `""` | VLM for image captioning |
| `compile.embedding.model` | `""` (opt-in) | Embedding model (`provider/model` or `provider:model`); empty disables vector indexing |
| `compile.output.format` | `okf` | Output format |

Set via `knox config set <key> <value>` or env vars (`KNOX_LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL`).
